<title>USA: AGA says U.S. weekly natgas stocks fell 130 bcf.</title>
<headline>AGA says U.S. weekly natgas stocks fell 130 bcf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Gas Association estimates of U.S. working gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):		    12/20/96  12/13/96  Net Chg  Pct Full(6)</p>
<p> Producing Reg. (1)	  498     550	-52     55</p>
<p> Consuming Reg. East (2)  1402    1464	-62     78</p>
<p> Consuming Reg. West (3)   292     308	-16     60</p>
<p> Total U.S.		   2192    2322     -130     69</p>
<p>Notes: (1) Incl Texas, Okla., Kansas, N.Mexico, Arkansas, Louisiana, and Miss. (2) Incl states east of Miss. River less Miss., plus Iowa, Neb and Missouri (3) Incl states west of the Miss. River less producing region and Iowa, Neb and Missouri.  </p>
<p>Survey sample and full working gas estimates</p>
<p> -			 Survey Sample   Est. Full Work-    Yr-Ago</p>
<p> -			 Size--Pct (4)   ing Gas--BCF (5)   Week</p>
<p> Producing Region	    70		    908	   629</p>
<p> Consuming Region East     83		   1790	  1259</p>
<p> Consuming Region West     96		    482	   390</p>
<p> Total U.S.		    81		   3180	  2278</p>
<p>Notes: (4) Ratio of max WG vol. to est. of highest WG in storage in past 2 yrs (EIA).(5) Highest WG level by state added to give regional and national levels (EIA).(6) Regional and total vols divided by est.full regional and total vols.</p>
</text>
